      "id": 477850,
      "username": "Vikashumar",
      "name": null,
      "created_at": "2025-08-18T10:18:52.047Z",
      "cooked": "<h3><a name=\"p-477850-h-1-use-the-erpnext-mobile-app-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477850-h-1-use-the-erpnext-mobile-app-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>1. Use the ERPNext Mobile App</strong></h3>\n<p>ERPNext has an official <strong>mobile app</strong> (Android &amp; iOS). Key points:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When creating or editing a document (like a <strong>Sales Order</strong>, <strong>Item</strong>, or a custom DocType), the <strong>Attach File / Attach Image</strong> field allows <strong>direct camera capture</strong>.</li>\n<li>The salesperson can take a photo on the spot, and it will be uploaded to ERPNext immediately.</li>\n<li>No extra coding required; works offline and syncs when online.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Recommended for:</strong> Quick deployment, minimal setup, real-time upload.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-477850-h-2-custom-web-form-with-camera-upload-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477850-h-2-custom-web-form-with-camera-upload-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>2. Custom Web Form with Camera Upload</strong></h3>\n<p>If you want the sales team to use a mobile browser instead of the app:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Create a <strong>Web Form</strong> in ERPNext for the DocType where photos are needed.</li>\n<li>Add a <strong>File / Attach Image field</strong>.</li>\n<li>Modern mobile browsers will allow <strong>“Take Photo”</strong> directly from the camera when attaching.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the DocType → Web Form → Add the fields you want.</li>\n<li>Ensure the <strong>Attach Image / File</strong> field is included.</li>\n<li>Share the link with salespeople; they can open it on mobile, take a photo, and submit.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Recommended for:</strong> Teams that don’t want to install the ERPNext app.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-477850-h-3-use-a-custom-mobile-integration-optional-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477850-h-3-use-a-custom-mobile-integration-optional-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>3. Use a Custom Mobile Integration (Optional)</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>If you need <strong>extra automation</strong>, e.g., auto-tagging photos with location, creating documents automatically, you can build a <strong>custom mobile app or Frappe REST API integration</strong>.</li>\n<li>This requires developer effort but gives full control.</li>\n</ul>",
